{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>תכבד</b> Two times in the Masorah: תכבד העבודה / כי יומם ולילה תכבד עלי ידך. Teaches that he burdened them by day and by night." "<b>ויעשו</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and elsewhere ויבאו ויעשו, and ויעשו בני ישראל את הפסח. As reward for this labor, they merited to make the Tabernacle and to offer a sacrifice." "<b>ישעו</b> Two times in the Masorah: ואל ישעו בדברי שקר / ישעו ואין מושיע. Those who do not direct their hearts in prayer and ישעו בדברי שקר — they do not intend in their hearts what they utter with their mouths — concerning them it is said: ישעו ואין מושיע. But those who intend in their hearts what they utter with their mouths, concerning them it is said: אז תקרא וה׳ יענה תשוע ויאמר הנני. And this is what David said: האזינה תפלתי בלא שפתי מרמה — when will You give heed to my prayer? When it is without lips of deceit. To contradict the heart and utter a thing not intended in one's heart." "<b>ויפץ</b> Three times in the Masorah: ויפץ העם / ויפץ ה׳ אותם / ויפץ העם מעליו concerning Saul. The latter — those dispersed to make bricks; and the men of the dispersion were dispersed on account of the sin of bricks, for they said הבה נלבנה לבנים. Just as in that dispersal their intent and their kingdom were nullified, so too the dispersal of the people from Saul caused him to hasten to offer the burnt offering before Samuel arrived — and this was the first cause for the nullification of Saul's kingdom."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:03.602201082Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}